  message: "Done via PR #384 (merged FF). supply_chain.TEST_FILE_PATTERNS gained Python test_*.py / *_test.py + bash test_*.sh suffix rules. Behavioral evidence (production-path classify_file, the item's filed gap): mymod/sub/test_thing.py, mymod/sub/thing_test.py, scripts/test_hooks.sh now classify tier=FIRST_PARTY, is_test=True (were is_test=False, reason 'default (no matching pattern)'). Additive — derived/external/generated precedence checks run first (unchanged); mirrors paths.is_test_file (startswith test_ / _test.). Core 100% coverage in isolation; CI passed. Latent on self-corpus (hypergumbo's own tests live under tests/ dirs, already caught by TEST_DIR_PATTERNS); surfaces on repos with co-located python/bash tests."  # 059a
